  "caption": "Quinn's hip started clunking with every leg lift, right after signing up for five dance classes a week.\n\nA snapping hip is often a tendon flicking over a bony bump, not the joint popping out. Painless snapping usually needs no treatment. Pain, catching and locking matter more than the noise.\n\nIf it's sore, what often helps: easing back on the move that sets it off while staying active, choosing gradual strengthening over hard stretching, and giving it a few weeks of sensible load changes.\n\nLocking, catching, deep groin pain or painful snapping that won't settle is worth getting assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
